247	 Other extension isolation remains ([ADR-0063](decisions/ADR-0063-loop-turns-without-personal-extensions.md)). Before each turn the adapter runs `codex mcp list --json` in the turn's working directory **with plugins switched off only for discovery**, so plugin-owned servers are not listed and then suppressed. It starts the turn with every listed standalone MCP server disabled (`mcp_servers.<name>.enabled=false`), with `features.apps`, `features.memories`, `features.hooks`, `features.multi_agent` (sub-agent spawning) and `features.goals` false, and with `notify=[]`. If the listing fails, the turn does not start. Plain `--config` overrides cannot clear a table such as `mcp_servers={}`, because the CLI merges them into the loaded configuration; standalone servers are therefore disabled by name and remain available through explicit node overrides.
248	 
249	-Configuration errors reported by the CLI retain their pre-submission refusal. Plugin inheritance follows normal CLI resolution, rather than checking package health: pinned CLI 0.160.0 silently skips unknown plugin IDs and missing plugin MCP files. A successful turn does not prove every configured plugin loaded; [#442](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/442) tracks diagnostics for that limit.
250	+Configuration errors reported by the CLI retain their pre-submission refusal. Plugin inheritance follows normal CLI resolution, rather than checking package health: pinned CLI 0.160.0 silently skips unknown plugin IDs and missing plugin MCP files. A successful turn does not prove every configured plugin loaded. System preflight adds an informational `plugins.codex` warning after Codex CLI/login readiness succeeds, and Settings shows the same scope notice in the Codex card (#442): loaded plugin tools are not verified by this check. Readiness, authentication, normal inheritance and node overrides remain unchanged. The notice starts no inventory, app-server or provider probe. Supported CLI inventory can help investigate, but configuration and tool lists do not establish complete loaded-plugin health; see [missing Codex tools](guide/07-troubleshooting.md#codex-plugin-tools-are-missing).
251	 
252	 Every listed server name and every segment of a node's override key must be one plain TOML key (letters, digits, `_`, `-`), and not `__proto__`, `constructor` or `prototype`. The shared contract checks raw authored keys before record parsing, including dotted keys, nested tables and tables inside arrays. The editor and API reject an invalid key with its field path instead of discarding it; publication also checks retained drafts and reports `CODEX_CONFIG_KEY_INVALID` on the inference node. Ordinary scalar values, valid tables and dotted keys keep their existing behavior. A previously stored invalid-key draft remains unchanged when publication is refused. Such stored definitions must be corrected before restarting with this contract, because the existing store guard refuses invalid definitions (see the CHANGELOG upgrade note).
