286	 ## First API key (Decided, WP-F2, ADR-0015)
287	 
288	 With `GG_REQUIRE_API_KEY=true`, `POST /api-keys` needs a key, so the first one cannot come from the API. Stop any API using the data directory first. `graphgoblin-api --create-api-key <name> [--scopes a,b]` (`node apps/api/dist/main.js ...`) reads the same environment as the server, takes its data-directory lock, creates the database if needed and applies migrations (as a start would), inserts a key for the local owner, prints the token once to standard output, releases the lock, and exits without starting the HTTP server. A held lock exits 1 before any database work. Nothing is logged; only the SHA-256 hash is stored. Scopes default to `*` only when `--scopes` is absent: an unknown or repeated option, a stray argument, a missing value, or a malformed scope exits 2 with the usage before anything is written. The install scripts print the command; in the container use `docker compose run --rm` with the API stopped, as shown in the guide.
